      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wealthy Louisvillians began building summer homes in Mockingbird Valley in 1905, starting with Atilla Cox's residence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mockingbird_Valley%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mockingbird Valley lies east of Louisville along the Ohio River, earning the nickname 'country enclave' for its rural feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mockingbird_Valley%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wild deer, coyotes, and red foxes frequently roam the forests and fields of Mockingbird Valley.",
